The homepage's random-apps listing (index.qmd): every app's slug as JSON,
for the "Surprise me" button to pick from. A listing rather than a list in
the script, so a new app is included with nothing to register. `<` is
escaped so nothing in the JSON can close the <script> early. The output tag
below is the equals one because Quarto's EJS writes that one raw and
escapes the dash one, the reverse of standard EJS.
*/ %>
<%
const apps = []
for (const item of items) {
  apps.push({slug: item.path.split("/")[2]})
}
%>
<script type="application/json" id="vm-random-apps"><%= JSON.stringify(apps).replace(/</g, "\\u003c") %></script>
